From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:26:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: bridge Signal reactions, replies and receipts to the
 transport

* Map Signal reactions to and from the transport

Incoming: a DataMessage carrying a reaction is not shown as a "Reacted
with X" line any more. It is forwarded as the "webos-im-reaction" signal
(target sent timestamp, emoji, reactor; an empty emoji removes it).
Every message stores its Signal id (sent timestamp in ms) on the
conversation as "webos-msg-id", including messages sent from another of
the user's devices, so a later reaction can find its target.

Outgoing: the transport emits "webos-im-send-reaction"; a handler sends
it as a DataMessage reaction, looking the target author up in the
message store. After a message sent from the app goes out, its server
id is reported back via "webos-im-outbox-id".

The signals are defined by the webOS imlibpurpletransport, so this is
not for upstream.

* Show Signal replies as inline quote cards

Incoming quotes are passed from Rust to C in the body behind a
\x01 id \x1f author \x1f text \x02 header. The C side strips it and
stores the parts on the conversation as webos-quoted-{id,from,text},
which the transport turns into a reply card.

For sending, the transport puts the reply target's id on the
conversation as "webos-reply-to"; presage_send_im/chat take it and the
Rust side builds the Signal Quote from the stored message.
presage_rust_send() gains a reply_to_ts argument for that.

* Report delivery and read receipts to the transport

Forward receipts for our outgoing messages as the "webos-im-receipt"
signal, one per target sent timestamp: delivery receipts as "delivered",
read and viewed receipts as "read". The messaging app shows them as
single and double ticks.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
